# TETHER 0.3.0: a clock on J1 and a reset on J2 when no MIDI clock comes in.
# CLOCK layout (J5 16ths, J6 reset). J1 at 4 PPQN (the default): one pulse a
# sixteenth. USB MIDI clock, when it comes, wins.
midi plug
wait 3000
expect booted
press b3
wait 400
tap b1
wait 100
pot 3 0.125                    # catch LAYOUT at BAND
wait 100
pot 3 0.375                     # CLOCK (zone 2 of 4: BAND, CLOCK, CV IN, CUSTOM)
wait 100
release b3
wait 200
mark
clock 1 125                    # J1: a pulse every 125 ms (120 BPM sixteenths)
wait 2010
expect edges 5 > 15            # sixteenths from J1
expect edges 5 < 18
expect edges 6 = 1             # the clock arriving started it: one RESET
# J2: a reset; the next pulse is the top of the bar
mark
pulse 2
wait 300
expect edges 6 = 1
# the clock stops: three of its periods later the transport stops
clock 1 0
wait 600
mark
wait 500
expect edges 5 = 0
# MIDI clock wins: J1 running at another tempo, MIDI's sixteenths come out
clock 1 50
wait 300
mark
midi start
midi clock 96 120              # 2 s of MIDI clock at 120 BPM
expect edges 5 > 14
expect edges 5 < 18            # MIDI's 16, not J1's 40
mark
pulse 2
wait 50
expect edges 6 = 0             # J2 ignored under MIDI clock
midi stop
clock 1 0
expect finite
expect alive
